  "notes": "Transcribed verbatim from FCC's official ACCJC Substantive Change Application for the New Baccalaureate Degree Program in Dental Hygiene (hosted on accreditation.fresnocitycollege.edu). program_type 'professional-phase': the document sequences ONLY the 62 upper-division units of the professional phase (Years 3-4: Junior/Senior). Students must complete a minimum of 60 degree-applicable units with CSU/IGETC certification BEFORE acceptance into the baccalaureate program; the lower-division admission prerequisites (21 units: English 1A/1AH, Communication 1 or 2, Statistics [Math 11/11H or Psych 42], Sociology 1A/1AH, Psychology 2/2H, Chemistry 3A, Chemistry 3B, BIOL 20 or 21A, BIOL 22 or 21B, BIOL 31) are carried in external_prereqs. Students completing the 60 lower-division units earn an AS in Pre-Allied Health. Total: 60 lower-division + 62 upper-division = 120 units for the Bachelor of Science in Dental Hygiene. The 62 upper-division units comprise 53 units of DH 700-series major courses and 9 units of upper-division general education (DH 700 Organizational Communication, DH 701 Medical Ethics Philosophy, DH 702 Anthropology), encoded as core/UD-GE. Semester sums verified: 14 + 16.5 + 16.5 + 15 = 62, matching the document's 'TOTAL PROGRAM UNITS 62'. The application states no per-course prerequisites within the professional phase (cohort model), so no prereq chains were encoded — none were invented. Admission is via lottery from applicants who completed all prerequisite coursework; 30 students accepted per year.",
